WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.280
A cell in your skin is not a neuron.

2
00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:08.340
Yet it helps a nerve keep firing while you press.

3
00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:10.160
This is the Merkel cell.

4
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:15.780
In mouse skin it sits in the basal epidermis, beside the ending of one slowly

5
00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.620
adapting type 1 afferent.

6
00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:23.340
Lineage tracing in mouse embryos shows it arises from epidermal progenitors, not

7
00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:24.340
from neurons.

8
00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:28.730
In cultured Merkel cells from young mice, pressing evokes a current.

9
00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:32.870
The current averaged 370 picoamps at its peak.

10
00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:38.590
At steady state it averaged 20 picoamps, about 5 .4 % of the peak.

11
00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:44.590
When Pietso II was deleted from skin epithelium, none of 13 cultured Merkel cells

12
00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:45.790
had a detectable current.

13
00:00:46.633 --> 00:00:49.133
So the cell's own current is mostly brief.

14
00:00:49.533 --> 00:00:53.073
Yet the afferent it drives fires for as long as the touch lasts.

15
00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:56.633
The dynamic phase is the fast firing at the onset.

16
00:00:57.133 --> 00:01:01.633
The static phase is the sustained firing that follows, with irregular intervals.

17
00:01:02.293 --> 00:01:06.173
How a brief current becomes sustained firing is not explained by these data.

18
00:01:06.967 --> 00:01:11.827
In an ex vivo mouse skin and nerve preparation, light that depolarizes only Merkel

19
00:01:11.827 --> 00:01:14.147
cells was enough to make the afferent fire.

20
00:01:14.967 --> 00:01:19.247
Light that hyperpolarizes them suppressed the sustained firing to a touch.

21
00:01:19.947 --> 00:01:24.867
In the reported experiment, from three units, median firing fell tenfold.

22
00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:31.200
In the mouse -2 receptor model, the miracle cell shapes the sustained firing, and

23
00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.980
the ending keeps its own mechanosensitive machinery.

24
00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:39.660
When piezo -2 was deleted from epithelium, dynamic responses stayed similar to

25
00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:42.840
controls and normal sustained firing was lost.

26
00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:48.540
In mice without miracle cells, afferents still respond to touch, but sustained

27
00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:49.940
firing is cut short.

28
00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:57.220
Peak firing fell from 238 to 79 Hz, down 66 .8 % in group means.

29
00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:01.380
A developmental deletion of the cells cannot say through which mechanism.

30
00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:04.850
What crosses the gap from cell to nerve?

31
00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:08.190
Three accounts exist, each in its own preparation.

32
00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:11.210
Noradrenaline, in mouse touch domes.

33
00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:13.770
Serotonin, in mouse whisker Merkel cells.

34
00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:18.150
Protons acting on ASIC channels, in rodent whisker follicles.

35
00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:21.410
The adrenergic account is neither settled nor refuted.

36
00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:27.330
Keep this: in mouse skin, a skin cell senses force, and its transmitter is still

37
00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:27.670
open.
